// The `typecheck` target's program: `tsc -p` over this package's .mjs and the
// JSDoc it carries, emitting nothing — checking is not a build step, so the
// shipped artefact stays directly loadable (AGENTS.md, "No TypeScript here,
// and why"). It extends the root tsconfig.base.json for `module: nodenext`,
// the same setting the boundary checker itself needs from that file: without
// it tsc cannot resolve the exports-map-only packages this code imports.
//
// - `skipLibCheck` — the target judges this package's JSDoc, not its
//   dependencies' shipped `.d.ts` files. Without it the run would fail on
//   upstream declaration conflicts nothing in this repository can fix.
// - `target: es2022` — decides only which library globals tsc assumes exist,
//   since nothing is emitted; es2022 is well inside this package's declared
//   `engines.node >=22`.
// - No `strict` — the gain this target buys is wrong JSDoc and wrong API
//   usage caught before review. Auditing the codebase for strict-null
//   soundness is its own pull request, not a flag flipped here.
{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "target": "es2022",
    "skipLibCheck": true
  },
  "include": ["**/*.mjs"]
}
